home=f'''<section class="hero"><div><img class="intro-profile-photo" src="/assets/srinivas-profile.jpeg" alt="Srinivas Gaddam" width="160" height="160"><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING NOTES BY SRINIVAS GADDAM</p><h1>Good architecture<br>starts with the<br><em>right trade off.</em></h1><p class="lede">Explore SoC design decisions across power, performance, area, latency and scalability. Practical articles, explicit assumptions and an interactive lab.</p><div class="actions">{button('/soc-architecture/','Explore the articles')}{button('/width-vs-frequency/','Open the lab',True)}</div><div class="authorline"><span class="avatar">SG</span><span><b>Srinivas Gaddam</b><br>Principal Engineer · SoC & high speed interfaces</span></div></div>{chip}</section><section class="dimensions"><div class="dimensiontitle">FIVE DIMENSIONS.<br>ONE SYSTEM.</div>{''.join(f'<div><b>{a}</b><span>{b}</span></div>' for a,b in [('P','Power'),('P','Performance'),('A','Area'),('L','Latency'),('S','Scalability')])}</section><section class="section"><div class="sectionhead"><div><p class="eyebrow">START WITH THE QUESTION</p><h2>From architecture to implementation.</h2></div><p>Work through the constraints, compare the options, and understand what would change the decision.</p></div><div class="featuregrid">{card('PART 01','Wider datapath or higher frequency?','A 512 bit datapath needs twice its useful throughput. Compare width, frequency and parallelism.','/soc-architecture/part-1/','SOC ARCHITECTURE')}{card('PART 01.1','Try the trade off yourself.','Change workload assumptions, shared bandwidth, power and area. See where each architecture becomes limited.','/width-vs-frequency/','INTERACTIVE LAB')}{card('PART 02','How Deep Should You Pipeline?','A 512 bit DMA aligner misses its 1.5 GHz timing target. Compare pipelining, rebalancing and restructuring.','/soc-architecture/part-2/','SOC ARCHITECTURE')}</div></section><section class="section pcieblock"><div class="sectionhead"><div><p class="eyebrow">PCIE SYSTEMS SERIES</p><h2>From power on to a usable device.</h2></div><a class="textlink" href="/pcie/">Explore the series →</a></div><div class="articlegrid">{pcards}</div></section><section class="aboutstrip"><span class="bigmonogram">SG</span><div><p class="eyebrow">THE ENGINEER BEHIND THE NOTES</p><h2>Implementation depth.<br>System perspective.</h2><p>Over 17 years working across SoC design, subsystem architecture and high speed interfaces. These notes connect architectural reasoning with the constraints of building silicon.</p><a class="textlink" href="/about/">Meet Srinivas →</a></div></section>'''
