soc=intro('SOC ARCHITECTURE / PPALS','Design choices.<br>System consequences.','A problem driven series on power, performance, area, latency and scalability. Start with a bandwidth decision, then test the assumptions in the lab.')+f'<section class="section"><div class="featuregrid">{card("PART 01","Wider datapath or higher frequency?","Compare three ways to double useful throughput, with workload and physical design assumptions made explicit.","/soc-architecture/part-1/")}{card("PART 01.1","Width vs Frequency","Explore the existing lab. Adjust constraints and inspect the model behind every result.","/width-vs-frequency/","INTERACTIVE LAB")}{card('PART 02','How Deep Should You Pipeline?','A 512 bit DMA aligner misses its 1.5 GHz timing target. Compare pipelining, rebalancing and restructuring.','/soc-architecture/part-2/','SOC ARCHITECTURE')}</div></section><section class="callout"><h2>PPALS is a system view.</h2><p>Here, performance means useful throughput. Latency tracks how long one operation takes. Scalability asks how effectively the architecture handles more work as resources grow.</p></section>'
write('soc-architecture/index.html',shell('SoC Architecture','Practical architectural trade offs across five dimensions.',soc,'soc'))
pcie=intro('PCIE GEN6 / GEN7','Follow the complete<br>device journey.','Four connected parts, from the first signs of life on the link to the address map a driver needs. Read them in order or start at the boundary that is failing.')+f'<section class="section"><div class="articlegrid">{pcards}</div><div class="actions">{button(NEWS,"Follow the LinkedIn newsletter",True)}</div></section>'
