about=intro('ABOUT THE AUTHOR','Srinivas Gaddam','Principal Engineer · SoC design · Subsystem architecture · High speed interfaces')+f'''<section class="profilelayout"><div class="profilecard"><span class="portrait">SG</span><h2>17+ years</h2><p>From architecture and RTL<br>to implementation.</p>{button(PROFILE,'Connect on LinkedIn')}</div><div class="prose"><h2>Connecting the block to the system.</h2><p>I am a Principal Engineer at Synopsys with over 17 years of experience in SoC design, subsystem architecture and high speed interfaces. My experience includes PCIe, UFS, UniPro, MIPI M-PHY, SATA, CPRI and Ethernet.</p><p>My work spans architecture and microarchitecture, RTL design, synthesis, low power design and verification, timing closure, logical equivalence checking and RTL to GDS implementation. That implementation experience shapes how I approach architectural decisions.</p><h2>Why this site exists</h2><p>SoC PPALS brings together practical design questions, worked examples and interactive experiments. Each article makes its assumptions visible and explains the conditions under which a decision is useful.</p><p>I have also served as an Engineering Manager and Design Lead, led and mentored ASIC engineers, and contributed to the MIPI M-PHY and UniPro specifications. I am exploring how AI assisted workflows can support design analysis and technical communication, with engineering review remaining essential.</p><h2>Areas of focus</h2><div class="tags"><span>SoC architecture</span><span>PCIe subsystems</span><span>RTL & microarchitecture</span><span>Power & performance</span><span>Interconnects</span><span>Implementation</span></div><p class="note">This is my personal technical site. The articles and lab do not disclose proprietary project details or represent an employer’s position.</p></div></section>'''
